[extension-namespaces/minting] Extension namespace minting (reviewing)
Artifact: proposals/extension-namespaces.md.
Mint extension namespaces using author-controlled absolute https URIs with unique paths below the controlled origin. Keep namespace identity exact and offline; validate recognized schema versions fail-closed; preserve unknown namespace payloads byte-exactly through parse and serialize.
-> core/freeze
> 2026-08-26: Extension namespace collision resistance comes from an author-controlled absolute https URI and a unique path below that origin; no registry, dereference, redirect resolution, or alias normalization participates in validation.
> 2026-08-26: Namespace identity is exact and offline; schema name and version are subordinate to the namespace and are not global bare names.
> 2026-08-26: A consumer that does not recognize a namespace retains its complete payload as opaque bytes; canonical serialization applies only to recognized schema values.
@artifact text/markdown ./proposals/extension-namespaces.md
---
[schemas/inventory] Minimal schema inventory (reviewing)
Artifact: proposals/schema-inventory.md.
The closed-algebra schema family that covers the empirical architecture cases without one schema per paper. Record allowed attachment kinds, candidate value bodies, coverage, minimality, and sized gaps. Preserve the boundary between finalized schema values and structural graph/projection semantics.
Accept: Every case-family row maps to a schema or an explicit gap; no paper-specific primitive is introduced; all candidate bodies use only the settled schema constructors.
-> extension-namespaces/minting
-> schemas/meta
